cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this platform, please cite it as below and cite the underlying tools."
title: "Four Therapeutic Strategies to Target Pancreatic Cancer: an open, end-to-end computational platform for drug discovery, drug repurposing, ADAR antisense guide design and peptide binders against KRAS mutants"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Nguyen
    given-names: Truong
    affiliation: "CUNY School of Medicine"
repository-code: "https://github.com/truong128/Four_therapeutic_strategies_to_target_Pancreatic_Cancer"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - KRAS mutants
  - pancreatic ductal adenocarcinoma
  - ultra-large virtual screening
  - machine learning
  - drug repurposing
  - antisense oligonucleotides
  - ADAR
  - RNA editing
  - peptide binders
  - Nextflow
abstract: >-
  Reproducible computational workflows against KRAS mutants: ML-guided docking of a 13.6 billion molecule
  library with resistance-aware ensemble docking, Boltz-2, molecular dynamics, MM/GBSA, OpenFE absolute binding free
  energy and retrosynthesis; repurposing of approved drugs across KRAS alleles;
  ADAR-recruiting guide RNA design with off-target and structure stages; and peptide binder design for 18
  KRAS alleles (mutants). Code and protocols only; no data or results are distributed.
